# Accepted container-image vulnerabilities.
#
# Same discipline as backend/.cargo/audit.toml: an entry claims the vulnerable
# code cannot run in this image, not that the finding is unimportant. Each names
# what would make the claim false, and scripts/tests/container_scan_exceptions_test.sh
# checks the claim against the build so it cannot outlive the facts.

# CVE-2026-14456 — OpenSSL denial of service via unbounded memory.
#
# libssl3 ships inside gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12 and Debian has published no
# fixed version, so there is nothing to upgrade to. It is also never loaded: the
# backend binary links neither libssl nor libcrypto, because every TLS path in
# the crate graph is rustls — sqlx `tls-rustls`, reqwest `rustls-tls`, lettre
# `tokio1-rustls-tls`. The only process in the image never opens the library.
#
# Revisit when Debian ships a fixed libssl3, or if any dependency switches to
# native-tls or openssl-sys, which the guard test refuses.
CVE-2026-14456

# CVE-2026-84782 — OpenSSL information disclosure (compat-openssl).
#
# The same library and the same reasoning as CVE-2026-14456 above. Debian lists
# libssl3 3.0.20-1~deb12u2 as affected with no fixed version, and the backend
# binary never loads it: on 2026-10-04 `ldd` of the release binary showed only
# libgcc_s, libm and libc, and neither openssl-sys nor native-tls is in the
# crate graph. The guard test checks this entry with the same assertions.
#
# Revisit when Debian ships a fixed libssl3, or if any dependency switches to
# native-tls or openssl-sys.
CVE-2026-84782
